<h2>Tree Plantation in Pakistan: A National Imperative</h2>
<p>Pakistan is among the top 10 countries most vulnerable to climate change, and tree plantation has become not just an environmental initiative but a national survival strategy. With deforestation rates alarmingly high and urban air quality deteriorating, the need for massive tree plantation in Pakistan has never been more urgent. ShajarDost stands at the forefront of this green revolution, having planted over 1.2 million trees across the country through community-driven plantation drives.</p>
<p>Tree plantation in Pakistan faces unique challenges: water scarcity, extreme heat, soil degradation, and limited public awareness. However, these challenges also present opportunities for innovative approaches like the Miyawaki method for urban forests, community-based mini nurseries, and educational programs like Green Scouts that train the next generation of environmental stewards.</p>
<h3>Why Tree Plantation Matters in Pakistan</h3>
<p>Pakistan has one of the lowest forest cover percentages in the world, at barely 5% compared to the international recommended minimum of 25%. This deficit contributes to devastating floods, extreme heat waves, soil erosion, and air pollution that affects millions of citizens. Every tree planted helps combat these issues by absorbing carbon dioxide, releasing oxygen, preventing soil erosion, and providing shade that reduces urban temperatures by several degrees.</p>
<h3>ShajarDost's Tree Plantation Approach</h3>
<p>Our approach to tree plantation in Pakistan is holistic and community-driven. We don't just plant trees and leave; we ensure long-term survival through maintenance programs, native species selection, and community engagement. Our plantations happen in schools, colleges, hospitals, parks, and community spaces where they provide maximum benefit to local populations. We prioritize native species like Neem, Amaltas, Kikar, and Shisham that are adapted to Pakistan's climate and require less water.</p>
<h3>How You Can Participate</h3>
<p>Whether you want to donate money for tree plantation, donate saplings, volunteer your time, or register for Mission 50 and plant 50 trees yourself, ShajarDost provides multiple pathways for participation. Every contribution, no matter how small, makes a difference in our mission to make Pakistan green.</p>
